<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>{{ privacy_policy_page_title }}</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 720px; margin: 4rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; color: #222; line-height: 1.55; }
    img.logo { max-height: 64px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
    .placeholder { background: #fffbe6; border-left: 4px solid #f0c419; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
    code { background: #f4f4f4; padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem; border-radius: 3px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
{% if privacy_policy_logo_path | length > 0 %}
  <img class="logo" src="/{{ privacy_policy_logo_filename }}" alt="Logo" />
{% endif %}
  <h1>{{ privacy_policy_page_title }}</h1>

  <div class="placeholder">
    <strong>Placeholder.</strong> This is the default page shipped by the
    <code>sabokit</code> privacy_policy bundle. Replace it with your
    organization's actual privacy policy:
    <ul>
      <li>Set <code>privacy_policy_html_path</code> in your Ansible vars to a
          local <code>.html</code> file.</li>
      <li>Optionally set <code>privacy_policy_logo_path</code> to your logo
          (PNG or SVG).</li>
      <li>Re-run the playbook.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>The bundle deploys a single nginx container behind Traefik with TLS
  via Let's Encrypt. No authentication is enforced — privacy policies must
  be reachable without login.</p>
</body>
</html>
